  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A man named Jake Barber, who has said he flew helicopters in a secret government program that recovers crashed craft of unknown origin, is judged by the guest Matthew Pines to be \"extremely credible\", with real professional credentials and \"entirely truthful\" about his experiences. Pines, speaking with Michels in 2025, stresses that Barber was essentially \"a delivery guy\": a helicopter pilot who knows what he saw and carried, but not someone told the bigger picture. That framing would mean Barber's account is real but limited to his own small part."
